diff --git a/docs/env_switches.tsv b/docs/env_switches.tsv
index 23625f5..293e88f 100644
--- a/docs/env_switches.tsv
+++ b/docs/env_switches.tsv
@@ -27,6 +27,7 @@ DM_DBG	diagnostic	When set, prints the guest's `svcOutputDebugString` text to st
 DM_DBG_AU_FRAMES	diagnostic	`=<frames>` asks the Mac's Core Audio output for that many frames per callback instead of about 5 ms (1024 reproduces the iOS default that caused crackling)
 DM_DETCLOCK	switch	`=<step ns>`: from the first present on, the guest clock advances a fixed step per present instead of following the wall clock, and the random source becomes a fixed-seed stream (replay and test runs)
 DM_DETCLOCK_PACE	switch	`=1` with `DM_DETCLOCK`: each frame takes at least one clock step of wall time, so background loading keeps up with the fixed clock (used by the screenshot gate)
+DM_DISPLAY_HZ	player	the launcher's frame-rate choice (settings.tsv): `60` or `120`, with an `L` suffix on the value lowering the render size; the iOS front end drives the present, the present link and the vi vsync event at the rate the screen holds (front_ios.m)
 DM_DISPLAY_NAME	switch	Overrides the iOS app's name in `build_ipa.sh` (default the game name in the base NSP's control data)
 DM_DYNAMIC_RESOLUTION	player	`1` lets NieR:Automata 1.0.3's own dynamic resolution scale between 70 and 100 %, `0` (default) keeps full resolution; only on the builds whose patches.py names the DYNAMIC_RESOLUTION capability (`hle_fpslock.c` `k_nier_dr`). The launcher's Dynamic resolution
 DM_ENTITLEMENTS	path	`=<plist>` gives a prepared Xcode project another entitlements file instead of the Increased Memory Limit one, and the ad-hoc signature of the unsigned IPA's executable carries them; empty means no entitlements
